  "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nAdd the LinuxCNC active comment guard to `assets/posts/tormach-lathe.cps` and `assets/posts/tormach-plasma.cps`.\r\nA comment opening with active keywords receives a leading `- `.\r\nThis keeps machine names and user comments inert on PathPilot controls.\r\n\r\nReason for new top-level test files: isolates post-specific active comment guards into focused binaries without bloating shared script golden suites.\r\n\r\n## Readings\r\n- Public LinuxCNC G-code manual on active comments.\r\n- `assets/posts/tormach.cps` reference implementation.\r\n\r\n## Pinning tests\r\n- `crates/post/tests/tormach_lathe_post.rs`\r\n- `crates/post/tests/tormach_plasma_post.rs`\r\n\r\n## What was not exercised\r\n- Physical machine execution on Tormach hardware.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Guard active comment keywords in Tormach lathe and plasma posts.\r\n\r\nFixes #4231\r\n",
